{
  "bridge_text": "Just as Mosk the fox sat there in his little green vest, he looked at Lina with eyes that seemed to hold many winters. Let us see what happens as she stands before him on those winding stairs.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree, Lina discovered a narrow curl of wooden stairs leading deep down into the dark. Sitting upon the very top step was an old grey fox wearing a patched green vest. This was Mosk. His voice sounded like dry autumn leaves skittering across stone as he warned her that the tree was no place for visitors. He told her to go home and forget the humming, but Lina shook her head, insisting she could not forget a song she had not yet heard."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With the numbers set aside, the fox remains poised on the step, his eyes fixed on the gift Lina left for him. He takes a breath and finally begins his journey down into the hollow.",
