{
  "bridge_text": "The firefly's light flickered low, leaving the fate of this tiny queen hanging in the balance like a starlit mystery. With bated breath, Lina knelt closer to see if the warmth of their presence might be enough to restore her glow.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "Mosk's whiskers trembled as he remembered the winter he failed to bring her medicine, leaving him guarding this tree in shame. He had been waiting so long for a chance to make things right. Lina knelt down, her eyes searching the queen's dimming light, and asked softly what the little creature needed to feel strong again."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "A drop of warm milk and a kind word, whispered the queen, for that was all medicine ever truly was. Mosk fetched the milk in a silver thimble and laid his furry paw gently beside her own. The queen's glow steadied, and the humming inside the tree blossomed into a tune Lina had never heard before, while Mosk, for the first time in years, hummed along."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

