{
  "bridge_text": "With the apple left behind as a sign of goodwill, the path forward seemed a little less guarded. The fox led the way down into the deep, echoing hollow.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming deepened into a quiet song. A firefly, large as a robin, lay motionless upon a bed of emerald moss, her once-bright glow flickering like a dying ember. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he looked down at her. He whispered that she had been his dearest companion once, but long ago, he had failed to bring her the medicine she needed. Ever since that winter, he had kept watch over the hollow, held captive by his own heavy heart and regret."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt beside the creature and gently asked what might mend her spirit. The queen murmured that a drop of warm milk and a kind word were all the medicine she required. Mosk hurried to fetch milk in a tiny thimble, placing his paw near hers with trembling care. As the queen drank, her golden light steadied and grew bright. The humming within the tree transformed into a melody Lina had never heard, and for the first time in years, Mosk hummed along, his voice finally finding peace."
    }
