{
  "bridge_text": "The weight of the past often keeps our words hidden, just as Mosk kept his secrets tucked away in the shadows of his heart. With that silence finally broken, the light within the hollow tree began to dance once more.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt before the firefly queen, her voice soft as she asked what the tiny ruler needed to heal. The queen whispered that a drop of warm milk and a kind word were all the medicine she ever required. Mosk, who had held his own painful regrets like a heavy stone for so long, carefully fetched the milk in a silver thimble. As he laid his paw beside Lina’s, the queen’s flickering glow steadied into a warm, golden pulse. The deep humming inside the tree shifted into a gentle, unfamiliar melody, and for the first time in many years, Mosk hummed along, letting the music wash away the silence he had kept for far too long."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s5"
